      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 41-year-old man was urgently admitted with sudden onset of chest pain. Emergency coronary angiography revealed a large aneurysm of the sinus of Valsalva and reduced blood flow in the left coronary artery. A modified Bentall operation and coronary artery bypass were performed successfully. A large sinus of Valsalva aneurysm should be regarded as a critical problem that could cause coronary insufficiency."},
